course: dictionary
lesson: 3788
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the context tells you which one the author means. «Footprint» is a good example: it can be a mark on the ground, or a way of talking about the harm we do to the planet.
explain: «It can be a bone or shell turned to stone, a print of a leaf, or even a footprint.» Here footprint means a mark left by a foot, because it sits in a list of things kept in rock. «Step out of the bath onto a dry floor and look at your wet footprint» uses the same meaning: the mark your foot leaves behind.
explain: Now read «a carbon footprint» in an environment lesson. There is no foot at all. A carbon footprint is the amount of harmful gas a person or thing adds to the air by using energy. Always test your meaning: put it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A footprint is a mark left by a foot or shoe on the ground, such as in sand, snow or mud.
fact: A carbon footprint is the amount of harmful gas a person or thing adds to the air by using energy.
fact: A footprint can also mean the space something takes up on the ground, like a building.
fact: Fossil footprints are traces kept in rock, and they show how dinosaurs walked.
fact: On the Moon, where there is no wind, footprints can last for millions of years.
exercise: «A fossil footprint in soft mud, filled with sand and hardened, can still be seen today.» What does footprint mean here? | A shoe that is too big | A gas that harms the air | The space a building takes up | *A mark left by a foot
exercise: «Her carbon footprint fell when she started cycling to school.» What does carbon footprint mean? | The number of steps she walks | The mark her shoes left in the mud | The size of her school building | *The amount of harmful gas added to the air by using energy
exercise: Sam says footprint always means a shoe mark. Which phrase shows a different meaning? | «Follow the footprints» in the snow | «Muddy footprints» on the carpet | *«Carbon footprint» for energy and air | «Leave footprints» in the sand
test: «The detective studied the footprints in the snow.» What does footprints mean? | Shiny stones | Buildings on a hill | Gases in the air | *Marks left by feet
test: «The factory's footprint covers the whole field.» What does footprint mean here? | Harmful gas added to the air | Trail of breadcrumbs | *Space a building takes up on the ground | Mark left by a foot
exam: «Use less energy to shrink your carbon footprint.» What does carbon footprint mean here? | The mark your shoe makes in mud | A famous dinosaur track | The space a school takes up | *The harmful gas we add to the air by using energy
